                            <comment id="15397020" author="vozerov" created="Thu, 28 Jul 2016 06:24:20 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Pavel, my comments:&lt;br/&gt;
1) I believe it should be fixed in Java first. Otherwise, when it is finally fixed in Java nobody will notify you about that and we will end up with semi-correct solution forever. Moreover, having several nodes in a single process is not only about tests. This could occur normally when integrating with other frameworks, when running inside application servers, etc.. We should implement it correctly right away. You may create a ticket for Java issue (as I understand, we need to add the same property to &lt;tt&gt;IgniteConfiguration.java&lt;/tt&gt;), and see if someone can pick it.&lt;br/&gt;
2) I am not sure that CPP code still works after your changes to JNI layer.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
